WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.079
What are the Council configurations?

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:07.200
To make decisions
in different policy areas,

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:09.519
the Council meets
in specialised meetings

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.759
known as Council configurations.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.039
Each configuration
is made up of ministers

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:16.360
from the member states.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.319
It is the ministers who vote
on behalf of their national government.

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:24.119
Each configuration
deals with specific issues.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:27.319
For example,
economic and finance ministers

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.280
meet to discuss financial affairs,

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.119
and ministers of justice
discuss justice issues.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.600
In total the Council of the EU meets

00:00:36.639 --> 00:00:38.759
in 10 different configurations.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.600
 There is no hierarchy
among Council configurations.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.159
However,
the General Affairs Council

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.680
and the Foreign Affairs Council

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.720
have specific roles
defined in the EU treaties.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.360
Meetings of each configuration
take place regularly.

00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:55.239
Some meet every month,

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:57.519
some 3-4 times a year,

00:00:57.839 --> 00:00:59.600
and some on an ad-hoc basis.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.239
Over a 150 preparatory bodies

00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:05.000
prepare the ground for the meetings.

00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:08.439
Meetings are chaired by the minister
from the member state

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:10.239
holding the Council presidency;

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:12.720
with the exception of
the Foreign Affairs Council,

00:01:12.879 --> 00:01:14.879
which is chaired by
the High Representative

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.600
of the Union for Foreign
Affairs and Security Policy.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:21.319
At their meetings,
ministers work together

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.360
to find common solutions
on issues of shared interest.

00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.519
The Council takes decisions
using simple majority,

00:01:28.959 --> 00:01:32.079
qualified majority or unanimity voting.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.680
When discussing or voting
on a legislative proposal,

00:01:35.879 --> 00:01:37.360
Council meetings are public.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.400
Meetings are also public

00:01:39.519 --> 00:01:41.600
when the Council is debating major issues

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:43.560
affecting the interests of the EU

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.119
and its citizens.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.600
Find out all you want to know

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.159
about Council configurations and much more

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.600
on Consilium.europa.eu

